course: dictionary
lesson: 15432
title: Words about numbers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone knows what they say is true. Statistical is one of them. It comes from statistics, which means collecting, counting and studying numbers to find patterns. «The report used statistical evidence from 500 children.» The word statistical tells you the report is based on numbers, not on one person's story.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «Our class ran a statistical survey of favourite fruits and made a bar chart.» Survey and chart are clues: both are about counting and showing numbers. Try the swap: "a survey of numbers" still makes sense, so statistical means about numbers gathered and studied.
explain: Statistical can also describe a link shown by numbers. «There is a statistical link between sleeping well and good marks.» One child who slept well and did well does not prove a link. Numbers from many children do. That is why scientists and newspapers say statistical when they want you to trust the numbers.
fact: Statistical means about statistics: the collecting, counting and studying of numbers and data.
fact: Statistical describes something shown by numbers rather than by single stories.
fact: «Statistical evidence» means proof made from numbers collected from many people or things.
fact: You often see statistical in maths with charts and averages such as the mean, median and mode.
fact: In the news, statistical tells you a claim is based on data, so you can ask how the numbers were collected.
exercise: «The class made a statistical chart of how they travel to school.» What does statistical mean here? | Shown by a single story | *Shown by counting and studying numbers | Shown by a drawing of a bus | Shown in colour only
exercise: «The team gathered data from 200 homes and wrote a statistical report.» Copy the word that tells you the report is based on numbers. | homes | wrote | team | *statistical
exercise: Mia says, «One child got fit by running, so running must make everyone fit.» Why is statistical evidence better proof? | It is one funny story | *It is shown by numbers from many children | It is a drawing of a runner | It is just a guess
test: «The statistical analysis showed that more children chose apples than pears.» What does statistical analysis mean? | Painting a picture of fruit | *Studying numbers to find patterns | Telling a funny story about apples | Guessing the answer quickly
test: Which sentence uses statistical in the right way? | I had statistical pizza for tea. | She ran statistical across the park. | *The newspaper printed statistical evidence about rain over ten years. | My statistical cat is very sleepy.
exam: «The statistical report showed the results clearly.» Which word is closest in meaning to statistical? | Musical | *Numerical, based on counted data | Hopeful | Magical
